[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Open Games (1...e5)"]
[Variation "Scotch Game: Classical Variation"]
[ECO "C45"]
[Character "positional,tactical"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "bishop-hits-knight,central-pawns"]
[Kind "sideline"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 { White opens the centre at once. } 3... exd4 { Take it: the pawn on d4 is not defended. } 4. Nxd4 4... Bc5 { Develops with an attack on the knight on d4. }
5. Be3
( 5. Nxc6 Qf6 { Attacks the knight on c6 and the pawn on f2 together. } 6. Qd2 dxc6 7. Nc3 Be6 )
( 5. Nb3 Bb6 6. Nc3 Nf6 )
5... Qf6 { Attacks the knight on d4 a second time. The queen is exposed, but White must keep defending the knight. }
6. c3 { Defends the knight on d4 with a pawn. } 6... Nge7 { Develops a knight without blocking the queen, and prepares to castle. }
7. Bc4 7... O-O { Castle: the king is safe and the rook joins in. }
8. O-O 8... Bb6 { Steps back before Nb3 can hit it, and still aims at d4. Plan: ...d6, ...Ne5 and ...Bf5. } *
